Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Keshaba of Devaliya in Gadhpur: Doubts over Luni Greens, the Miracle of the Bolster, and Divine Darshan After embracing the Swaminarayan faith, Keshaba, the royal mother of the illustrious chieftain Darbar Jalamsinh of Devaliya, arrived in Gadhada for the very first time to seek the holy darshan of Bhagwan Swaminarayan.
Accustomed to royal luxury, aristocratic pride, wealth, and worldly authority, she entered the inner court of Dada Khachar&rsquo;s Darbargadh. Shreeji Maharaj was seated upon a cot on the northern veranda, surrounded by eminent paramhansas including Sadguru Muktanand Swami, Paramchaitanyanand Swami, Atmanand Swami, and Nishkulanand Swami. Beside Maharaj rested a large woven wicker basket filled with raw, freshly harvested wild purslane greens (luni bhaji). Reaching His hands into the basket, Shreeji Maharaj casually picked up bunches of greens, biting into them raw and chewing them with natural simplicity.
Observing this unpretentious, human-like activity, Keshaba felt deeply scandalized. Rising haughtily from the women&rsquo;s section, she murmured in disgust: &ldquo;Can this person possibly be God? He displays not the slightest hesitation or decorum before such a distinguished gathering! What an uncouth manner of eating! Even a simple peasant washes, sorts, and cooks vegetables before eating, whereas He grabs raw wild greens like cattle and chews on them with His bare teeth! Who could consider Him divine? He appears foolish and uncultured. We traveled all the way from Devaliya only to waste our time!&rdquo;
Agitated and perturbed, she prepared to march back to her guest quarters. Perceiving her departure, omniscient Shreeji Maharaj instructed His personal attendant: &ldquo;Brahmachariji! Inquire why that royal lady rose so abruptly. Go find out if she is distressed or remembered some urgent chore!&rdquo;
Mulji Brahmachari rushed forward and inquired gently: &ldquo;Mother! Why are you walking away so upset? Shreeji Maharaj affectionately inquires if you are facing any difficulty.&rdquo;
Keshaba retorted disdainfully: &ldquo;Enough! I have seen both your Maharaj and you! People throughout the country praise Him as the Supreme Lord, which is why I came for darshan. But seeing Him here, I realize you are all deluded! How could someone who lacks even basic etiquette and civilized eating habits be the Almighty God?&rdquo;
Mulji Brahmachari responded with a gentle, patient smile: &ldquo;Mother, pray dispel this illusion of your worldly gaze! Cleanse your inner heart and observe with genuine spiritual discernment; only then will His divine reality become evident. Do not act in haste. Return and investigate with patience! Having arrived with sacred faith, one cannot fathom the Supreme Being through frantic judgments.&rdquo; Persuaded by Brahmachari&rsquo;s calm conviction, Keshaba and Darbar Jalamsinh returned to the congregation.
A short while later, Shreeji Maharaj stood upon the veranda granting darshan to all. As Keshaba observed Him, Maharaj playfully took a large bolster pillow (takiyo) into His hands, tossing it upward repeatedly. Suddenly, from a considerable distance, He flung the heavy bolster toward His cot situated under the shade of the neem tree. To everyone&rsquo;s astonishment, the bolster flew gracefully through the air and landed with flawless precision right at the headrest position, as though carefully placed by hand!
A lightning spark of awe ignited in Keshaba&rsquo;s heart: &lsquo;Good heavens! What superhuman precision! Surely He is no ordinary mortal; He must be an exalted divine personality! I erred gravely in judging Him with premature haste.&rsquo; Sitting among the female devotees, she gazed intently upon Maharaj. In that transcendent moment, Shreeji Maharaj unveiled His divine, sixteen-year-old spiritual form, radiating celestial golden brilliance and adorned in resplendent golden-threaded garments! The divine ecstasy of that celestial vision washed away every trace of doubt and arrogance from her heart.
Tears of devotional joy welled up in her eyes. Turning to her son, she confessed emotionally: &ldquo;Son Jalamsinh! In this human lifetime, we need never look elsewhere! Look upon Him! Beholding His true divine form, every shred of my delusion has vanished into thin air. The sovereign divinity within Him is boundless; His playful human-like leelas are beyond mortal comprehension. A finite soul cannot decipher Him in haste. Take me immediately to His lotus feet so that we may take our vows and wear the sacred kanthi!&rdquo;
Mother and son prostrated before Shreeji Maharaj and formally received initiation. Keshaba spent five blissful days in Gadhada, listening to divine discourses. Smiling warmly, Mulji Brahmachari remarked: &ldquo;Mother! Look, does a mango ripen in a hurry? Just as one cannot sow seeds today and reap the harvest tomorrow, spiritual realization demands patient devotion.&rdquo;
Keshaba laughed softly and acknowledged with deep humility: &ldquo;You spoke the absolute truth, Brahmachariji! I have now fully realized my mistake.&rdquo;
