Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The Mango Tree of Gop Village, a Farmer&rsquo;s Selfless Offering, and Shreeji Maharaj&rsquo;s Prophecy of Liberation In the village of Targhari Devaliya within the Halar province, the tradition of pure devotional Satsang had flourished since the time of Sadguru Ramanand Swami. From this devout town, a party of four devotees led by the noble chieftain Darbar Modjibhai set out on foot toward Gadhada to seek the holy darshan of Bhagwan Swaminarayan.
En route, night fell as they reached the outskirts of Gop village, and they camped upon the soft, sandy banks of the local river. Rising at dawn, they bathed in the flowing river and sat upon the sands to perform their daily prayers and meditation. Across the bank in a riverside orchard, they noticed a lush mango tree laden with ripe, golden fruit. An affectionate wish arose in their hearts to offer these succulent mangoes to Shreeji Maharaj.
Just then, the peasant owner of the orchard approached. Modjibhai called out: &ldquo;Brother! Pray pluck four ripe mangoes for us, and take whatever price you deem appropriate.&rdquo;
The farmer inquired curiously: &ldquo;To whom do you intend to present these mangoes?&rdquo;
Darbar Modjibhai replied with reverence: &ldquo;We are carrying them as an offering to our spiritual master, the manifest Supreme Lord, Bhagwan Shree Swaminarayan.&rdquo;
Hearing the sanctified name of the Lord, the farmer&rsquo;s heart was softened with unbidden reverence. He personally climbed up, selected four prime, naturally ripened mangoes, and placed them into their hands, insisting: &ldquo;I desire no money for these; pray present them to the Almighty on my behalf.&rdquo;
Rejoicing, the devotees journeyed to Gadhada and entered Dada Khachar&rsquo;s Darbargadh. Prostrating before Shreeji Maharaj, they placed the four golden mangoes upon His cot and took their seats before Him. The omniscient Lord smiled and asked: &ldquo;From where did you obtain these magnificent mangoes?&rdquo;
Modjibhai narrated humbly: &ldquo;O Maharaj! As we rested by the river at the outskirts of Gop village, we sought to purchase them. But upon learning that they were meant for You, the humble farmer gave them freely with pure, selfless devotion.&rdquo;
Pleased with the farmer&rsquo;s pure sentiment, Shreeji Maharaj sliced one mango and relished it with evident delight, proclaiming: &ldquo;We have partaken of mangoes across Gujarat, Kathiyawad, and Sorath, but never have We tasted a mango as exceptionally sweet as this!&rdquo;
Witnessing this, His witty and beloved companion, Sadguru Brahmanand Swami, humorously interjected to procure prasad: &ldquo;Maharaj! Only the one who eats it knows whether it is truly sweet or sour! How are we bystanders to fathom its sweetness?&rdquo;
Laughing merrily at Swami&rsquo;s affectionate banter, Shreeji Maharaj gave one mango to Brahmanand Swami, another to Dada Khachar, and the third back to Modjibhai and his companions as sanctified prasad.
Brahmanand Swami then folded his hands and inquired thoughtfully: &ldquo;O Lord! You, the Supreme Godhead, have partaken of this mango; I, Your ascetic, have eaten it; and divine devotees like Dada Khachar have relished it. What spiritual destiny shall befall the farmer who grew this fruit?&rdquo;
The omniscient Lord pronounced a profound prophecy: &ldquo;Within six months, that mango tree will wither and dry up, and its owner too will cast off his mortal frame. Both soul and tree will take birth in pious Satsangi families, lead virtuous lives as exemplary devotees, and ultimately attain eternal liberation in Our divine Akshardham!&rdquo;
Following the Bhim Ekadashi festival, the devotees returned home. Months later, after attending the grand Diwali, Prabodhini Ekadashi, and Kartiki Purnima festivals in Gadhada, they passed once again through the outskirts of Gop village. Looking toward the riverbank, they noticed the mango tree was missing. Inquiring of the local villagers, they were told: &ldquo;That mango tree withered away completely, and its peasant owner passed away just two days ago!&rdquo;
The devotees were filled with profound veneration. Witnessing the literal fulfillment of Shreeji Maharaj&rsquo;s prophecy, their conviction deepened that even an inanimate tree or an unsuspecting soul whose offering is sanctified by the Lord or His exalted sants attains supreme spiritual liberation.
- From &lsquo;Shree Haricharitramrut Chintamani&rsquo;&hellip;
