Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Deliverance of a Ghost in Vadthal, a Devout Widow&rsquo;s Feast, and Shreeji Maharaj&rsquo;s Discourse on Overcoming Desires Gam arere gaye sukhasindhu, Memdavadme aaye deenbandhu&hellip;! Gam Vadthal sunj he saare, Dadusarme Prabhuji padhare&hellip;!! - From Shree Harivicharan Granth, Vishram 4
Traveling with an entourage of sants and devotees across the Charotar and Kheda territory, Bhagwan Swaminarayan arrived at the village of Vadthal in Mahudha taluka. Yielding to the affectionate pleadings of local seekers, the Lord agreed to camp there overnight. After concluding the evening arti and devotional prayers, Shreeji Maharaj was seated amidst the congregation, delivering divine spiritual discourses.
Suddenly, a grieving widow from the village walked up to the assembly, offered prostrations from a distance, and pleaded through streaming tears: &ldquo;O Lord! Pray banish my agonizing distress!&rdquo;
Hearing her desperate cry, the all-merciful Lord walked over accompanied by two elderly village devotees and asked: &ldquo;Speak, sister! What profound sorrow afflicts you?&rdquo;
Weeping bitterly, the woman revealed her plight: &ldquo;O Maharaj! My husband passed away some time ago, leaving me widowed and childless. Recently, he has begun appearing before me in the dark of night in the ghastly form of a phantom (pret). He torments me incessantly, confessing that because of deep unfulfilled sensual and worldly attachments (vasana), he is trapped as a restless ghost. Overcoming my terror, I mustered courage and asked him what righteous deed I could perform to liberate him from this cursed existence. He answered: &lsquo;My liberation will only be possible when Bhagwan Shree Swaminarayan and His ascetic sants visit Vadthal. You must lovingly prepare a sumptuous feast for the Lord and His sants, perform worship with clothes and ornaments, and wrap pure garments around the sadhus. Only then shall I be freed! If you fail to do this, I will take your life! We have no lineage to inherit our wealth; if you do not spend it in this holy cause, strangers will usurp it and your fate will be dreadful.&rsquo; Therefore, O Merciful Lord! Pray accept my devotional feast and deliver my tormented husband from the ghostly realm!&rdquo;
Listening intently to her sorrowful account, Shreeji Maharaj turned toward the entire gathering and pronounced a solemn sermon on spiritual detachment: &ldquo;Behold the terrible plight wrought by worldly attachments! Intense clinging to wealth, material assets, and sensual pleasures plunges the departing soul into such wretched degeneration. Therefore, let every true seeker rigorously burn away inner vasana, cultivate unalloyed detachment (nirvasanik state), and anchor their soul exclusively in the refuge of God.&rdquo;
Testing her depth of faith, Maharaj initially demurred: &ldquo;Sister, We must depart in haste and cannot linger to dine. At some future time when We return, We shall certainly partake of your feast.&rdquo;
At these words, the widow fell into despair and wept inconsolably. Moved by her distress, the local devotees interceded with folded hands: &ldquo;O Lord! Have mercy! You cannot depart without dining at this suffering sister&rsquo;s home. It is solely for the redemption of bound souls that You and these exalted ascetics wander upon this earth. Pray accept her offering!&rdquo;
Yielding to their heartfelt prayers, Shreeji Maharaj consented. The following morning, pious Brahmins prepared a sanctified feast of rich sweets, savory lentils, vegetables, and warm rotlis. Offering the sacred food to Thakorji, Shreeji Maharaj relished the meal and then personally supervised the feeding of all the ascetics and attendants.
Maharaj then instructed the sants: &ldquo;O Sants! Having partaken of this food, immerse your souls in devout meditation and pray earnestly: &lsquo;O Lord, bestow ultimate redemption upon this departed spirit, and grant eternal spiritual liberation to this noble sister who has offered this feast!&rsquo;&rdquo;
The sants prayed with pure devotional fervor. The pious woman then performed reverent worship of Shreeji Maharaj, adorning Him with ornaments and presenting fine white garments to all the ascetics. By the sovereign grace of Bhagwan Swaminarayan, the husband&rsquo;s spirit was instantly liberated from the realm of ghosts, and all torment ceased forever. Bestowing His divine blessings upon the village, Shreeji Maharaj resumed His journey toward Umreth.
- From &lsquo;Satsang Stri-Ratnamala&rsquo;&hellip;
