Acharya Ayodhyaprasadji Maharaj composed numerous devotional hymns imbued with profound love for Shreeji Maharaj and inspired Sadguru Bhumanand Swami to author the monumental scripture &lsquo;Ghanshyam Lilamrutsagar&rsquo;. His contemporary, the revered devotee Anandjibhai, recounted: &ldquo;Whoever came into contact with Acharya Ayodhyaprasadji Maharaj attained spiritual fulfillment; His gracious glance alone subdued the inner enemies of ego, anger, and worldly desire!&rdquo;
Acharya Maharaj possessed boundless compassion for devotees. When Kakabhai, a devotee in Ahmedabad, was embroiled in a fabricated legal lawsuit, Acharya Maharaj hired an eminent barrister from England at immense expense to secure his complete exoneration.
A particularly memorable incident illustrates his vigilant protection of devotees and the indomitable faith of a young Patidar seeker. A devout Patidar family had arranged the wedding of their son to the daughter of an affluent gentleman of the same caste. Unknown to them, the bride&rsquo;s father harbored bitter malice toward the Swaminarayan Sampradaya. He secretly plotted to humiliate the family: &lsquo;When the wedding procession arrives at the altar, I will coerce the groom to renounce the Swaminarayan fellowship before the entire assembly, or else I will dismiss the wedding procession, subjecting them to public disgrace.&rsquo;
Sensing this insidious design, the anxious father hurried to Ahmedabad and laid his predicament before Acharya Shree Ayodhyaprasadji Maharaj with tearful eyes.
Acharya Maharaj comforted him reassuringly: &ldquo;Fear not; Shreeji Maharaj will preserve your honor.&rdquo; Maharaj immediately summoned another wealthy and staunch Patidar devotee from the same clan and instructed him in private: &ldquo;If that antagonistic father refuses to marry his daughter to this devotee youth at the wedding canopy, you must immediately step forward and wed your eligible daughter to this groom at that very hour! Under no circumstances must this Satsangi&rsquo;s wedding procession return humiliated!&rdquo; The faithful devotee humbly bowed to the preceptor&rsquo;s command and gladly agreed.
On the appointed day, the marriage procession arrived at the venue amidst joyful celebrations. When the auspicious hour for circumambulating the sacred fire arrived, the bride&rsquo;s hostile father stepped into the center of the mandap and shouted arrogantly: &ldquo;If you wish to marry my daughter, declare loudly before this entire gathering: &lsquo;I am not a follower of Swaminarayan!&rsquo; Otherwise, take your procession and leave in shame!&rdquo;
A tense silence fell over the gathered guests. Without the slightest fluster, the radiant young groom replied with calm composure: &ldquo;Father-in-law! Has the entire community gathered? Only men seem present; pray call the women of the household as well.&rdquo; Intrigued, the entire contingent of village women gathered around the canopy.
Addressing his mother-in-law, the courageous young groom asked politely: &ldquo;Mother-in-law! Before this entire gathered clan, pray proclaim just one sentence: &lsquo;This man who is my father-in-law is not your husband!&rsquo; Your marital relationship may continue as it is; simply utter this one sentence publicly before our people!&rdquo;
The mother-in-law gasped in shock: &ldquo;Son-in-law! What madness are you demanding? How can I ever utter such a vile untruth before the entire community about the man who is truly my lawful husband?&rdquo;
Hearing her emphatic refusal, the lion-hearted youth declared with resounding conviction: &ldquo;Hear this, elders and relatives! If my mother-in-law cannot utter a simple lie about a mortal husband of transient flesh and bone, how could I ever commit the unpardonable sin of disowning the Almighty Supreme Lord Bhagwan Swaminarayan, the eternal master of my soul, merely to secure a mortal bride? Not once, but a thousand times over, I belong to Bhagwan Swaminarayan! If you do not wish to give your daughter, I have no desire to marry her either!&rdquo; With these fearless words, he stepped away from the altar.
Witnessing his extraordinary integrity, the community elders sternly rebuked the bride&rsquo;s father: &ldquo;You fool! If this noble, virtuous young man leaves this altar, another family is waiting to offer their daughter in marriage, whereas your family will be permanently disgraced and your daughter will remain unwed!&rdquo;
Overwhelmed with shame and fear, the bride&rsquo;s father fell at the young man&rsquo;s feet, begged forgiveness, and joyfully completed the wedding rituals. Through Acharya Ayodhyaprasadji Maharaj&rsquo;s visionary foresight and the young man&rsquo;s unyielding faith, the glory of Satsang was triumphantly vindicated.
- From the biographical episodes of Acharya Shree Ayodhyaprasadji Maharaj&hellip;
