The Fruits of Ethics: Shreehari unequivocally proclaimed: &ldquo;He who walks steadfastly upon the path of righteousness and moral integrity invariably enjoys perennial peace and happiness, which is evident for all to behold. Conversely, one who indulges in deceit, unethical conduct, and adharma plunges into immense misery without delay!&rdquo;
Spiritual Discretion as the Primary Fruit of Satsang: Worldly joy and sorrow are experienced directly by everyone. Among these, the person bereft of spiritual discretion (vivek) endures continuous affliction. Even if a person practices Satsang for millions of years, genuine peace remains elusive unless he cultivates true discretion.
