Foreseeing future events, omniscient Shreehari delivered a solemn warning: &ldquo;Adabhai! What if an adverse period of severe drought arrives when even the local farmers have no fodder left for their own oxen? They will inevitably tell you to take your livestock back. If you are returning home with belongings loaded upon your horse and the exhausted animal collapses and dies of starvation on the roadside, you will be forced to carry the heavy saddle upon your own head on foot! Where will your royal dignity be then? Therefore, undertake no new construction, and do not purchase additional buffaloes or horses! If you abide by Our words, you will prosper.&rdquo;
