Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Kariyani: Minbai&rsquo;s Supreme Devotion - Breaking Water Pot in Torrential Rain to Feed Shreehari During His stay in Kariyani, the monsoon season brought an unprecedented deluge. Dark, thunderous clouds engulfed the skies, unleashing torrential rains accompanied by deafening lightning. Pathways turned into surging torrents.
In the midst of this furious downpour, Shreeji Maharaj arrived drenched at the humble doorstep of His devoted disciple, Minbai. Astonished to see the Lord soaking wet, Minbai exclaimed: &ldquo;O Maharaj! We householders wander restlessly out of worldly greed, but what worldly wealth do You need to amass that You roam in such a storm? Pray sit comfortably and rest!&rdquo;
Shreehari replied with playful tenderness: &ldquo;Minbai! Having assumed a human frame, the body requires sustenance! The rains flooded Our lodging and hunger struck Us; spotting your hut nearby, We ran here!&rdquo;
Minbai offered a dry cloth and seated Maharaj upon a cot. However, rainwaters had seeped into the kitchen, extinguishing the clay hearth. Without a moment&rsquo;s hesitation, Minbai emptied a large earthen water pot (matlu) and split it in half, filling the base with dried cow dung and embers to fashion an improvised indoor stove!
Seeing this, Shreehari remarked: &ldquo;Minbai! What have you done? How will you fetch water without your pot?&rdquo; Minbai replied with boundless love: &ldquo;O Lord! The potter&rsquo;s house is nearby; I can buy another pot tomorrow morning. But where will I ever find this blessed opportunity of feeding Purna Purushottam Narayan at my humble home? Wealth can always be regained, but such a divine moment never returns!&rdquo;
Minbai prepared a piping-hot, fluffy bajra rotlo, made deep impressions filled with rich melted ghee, and served it with fresh curd, sweet butter, and pickles. Overwhelmed by her unadulterated love, Shreehari relished the feast with supreme joy.
