Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Ravjibhai of Kala Talav and the Mouse Incident Departing from the village of Tera in Kutch, Shriji Maharaj arrived in the evening at the home of carpenter Ravjibhai in the village of Kala Talav and seated Himself comfortably in the veranda.
At that time, Ravjibhai&rsquo;s wife was sitting inside an inner room alongside her mother-in-law. Suddenly, a small mouse darted into the room. Terrified at the sight of the mouse, the woman sprang to her feet and ran outside in panic.
Witnessing this, Shriji Maharaj laughed and remarked, &ldquo;If you are so terrified of a tiny mouse, what will you do when the fierce messengers of Yama (Yamadutas) arrive at your end time?&rdquo;
The devoted woman replied with instinctive, unshakeable conviction, &ldquo;O Maharaj! When we have attained You—the Supreme Almighty Himself—what harm can those wretched messengers of Yama dare do to us?!&rdquo;
Hearing her resolute faith, Shriji Maharaj was immensely pleased and proclaimed, &ldquo;If you maintain such unwavering conviction in Us forever, the messengers of Yama will never dare approach you!&rdquo;
Saying this, Maharaj sat down to take His evening meal. The devoted lady affectionately served warm millet rotla, fragrant clarified butter (ghee), and jaggery. Having relished the meal and rested briefly, Maharaj departed and arrived at the coastal port of Mandvi.
In Mandvi, Maharaj resided for a month at the residence of dedicated devotees, including Khaiya Khatri. There, He delivered profound discourses on dharma, spiritual knowledge, detachment (vairagya), and personal duties, revealing His supreme divine identity: &ldquo;O devotees! I am the Supreme Source of all divine incarnations (Avatarna Avatari) and the eternal resident of Akshardham. Solely for the supreme redemption of souls, I manifested through Bhaktimata and Dharmadev in the village of Chhapaiya in Kaushal, and undertook seven long years of austere forest pilgrimage on foot before arriving here. By meditating upon My divine form and chanting My holy name, the soul is forever liberated from the agony of the cycle of birth and death and the horrors of dwelling in the womb. Understanding My transcendent glory, worship Me unceasingly.&rdquo;
Imparting these sublime teachings, Maharaj departed from Mandvi. En route, He bathed in the Hari Sarovar near Dahisara, quenched His thirst, rested briefly, and graced the devotees with His darshan before arriving in Bhujnagar. In Bhuj, Maharaj lodged on the upper floor of Gangarambhai&rsquo;s residence, where countless devotees gathered to behold His divine darshan.
From &lsquo;Shri Kutch Leela&rsquo;, Chapter 59&hellip; 🙏
