Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The Sons of Mavji Dave of Dhoraji and Shriji Maharaj In the town of Dhoraji, the foundation of Satsang had been firmly established since the era of Gurudev Ramanand Swami. Ramanand Swami frequently graced Dhoraji with his presence and stayed at the residence of his ardent Brahmin devotee, Mavji Dave. In Dhoraji, Swami had also instituted an alms-house (sadavrat), which Mavji Dave managed selflessly, feeding sadhus, pilgrims, and guests with utmost reverence.
After Shri Hari ascended the spiritual throne, He too visited Dhoraji frequently, convening large spiritual assemblies at Lalvado. Through numerous divine miracles and displays of divine majesty, He instilled unshakeable conviction of His supreme Purushottam status in the hearts of all spiritual seekers.
Once, Shri Hari arrived in Dhoraji accompanied by a congregation of devotees and senior sadhus, including Sadguru Muktanand Swami. The local Khimani Darbars lovingly hosted Shri Hari. In the assembly that day, Mavji Dave&rsquo;s widowed sister, Ganga Bahen, brought her four young nephews to have darshan of Shri Hari.
Bowing at Shri Hari&rsquo;s lotus feet, Ganga Bahen petitioned with folded hands, &ldquo;O Lord! I am like a withered leaf; my frail body will not last much longer. These are the four sons of my late brother Mavji Dave—Harjivan, Raghavji, Valji, and Keshavji. My brother has already departed for Your divine abode, and I have raised these four orphans. Now that You have arrived today, I surrender them unto Your holy lotus feet. Whether my mortal body survives or not, please look after them eternally.&rdquo;
Casting a benevolent glance upon the four brothers, Shri Hari comforted her, &ldquo;Ganga Bahen! Whoever surrenders to Us, We constantly bear their protection and care. Mavji Dave was immensely dear to Gurudev Ramanand Swami; therefore, do not harbor the slightest anxiety.&rdquo;
Saying this, Shri Hari asked the young boys, &ldquo;Have you studied anything?&rdquo; The eldest, twelve-year-old Harjivan, nodded &lsquo;yes&rsquo;, while the three younger brothers shook their heads &rsquo;no&rsquo;.
Shri Hari immediately turned to Sadguru Muktanand Swami and said, &ldquo;Swami, if you have a scripture with you, let us gift it to these boys.&rdquo;
At that time, Muktanand Swami was reading a handwritten manuscript of the Ramayana. Shri Hari requested four sections (kands) of the epic. Excluding the eldest, Harjivan, Shri Hari placed one kand into the hands of each of the three younger boys!
Beholding this, everyone in the assembly was astonished, and murmurs broke out: &ldquo;Maharaj&rsquo;s ways are truly perplexing! Harjivan is educated, yet he was given nothing, whereas the three younger, uneducated boys were gifted sections of the sacred Ramayana!&rdquo;
Just then, at Shri Hari&rsquo;s divine command, the three unlettered young boys began reciting the chaupais of the Ramayana with flawless, fluent pronunciation! Witnessing illiterate children reciting the sacred Sanskrit and Avadhi verses with such effortless eloquence, the entire assembly was spellbound with awe.
Shri Hari proclaimed, &ldquo;Ganga Bahen, these young boys now know how to recite the Ramayana fluently; therefore, their worldly livelihood will proceed smoothly and honorably.&rdquo; Ganga Bahen bowed in deep gratitude.
Sadguru Muktanand Swami folded his hands and asked, &ldquo;O Lord! Your divine lilas are unfathomable, beyond the comprehension of mortal beings. You blessed these three younger boys with the Ramayana, but why did You leave the eldest, Harjivan, empty-handed?&rdquo;
Shri Hari smiled gently and replied, &ldquo;Swami, We acted as We deemed appropriate.&rdquo; Muktanand Swami reflected in his heart that God&rsquo;s supreme will is beyond question; whatever Maharaj does is ultimate wisdom. In this manner, Shri Hari dispelled Ganga Bahen&rsquo;s worries.
Eight to ten months later, Shri Hari revisited Dhoraji via Varjang Jaliya alongside Muktanand Swami. Young Raghavji came for darshan and offered prostrations. Omniscient Shri Hari, knowing everything within His heart, asked, &ldquo;Raghavji, what is your elder brother Harjivan doing?&rdquo;
Young Raghavji replied with tears, &ldquo;O Maharaj! Six months after You visited us last time, elder brother Harjivan departed for Your eternal divine abode!&rdquo;
Hearing this, Shri Hari immediately glanced toward Sadguru Muktanand Swami. Swami instantly understood the profound truth: Harjivan&rsquo;s earthly lifespan was drawing to a close, so Maharaj had absorbed his soul directly into Akshardham; whereas the three younger brothers were destined to live long and were blessed with the recitation of the Ramayana to sustain their earthly livelihoods! Overwhelmed with reverence, Muktanand Swami bowed before the Lord, singing verses praising His omniscient wisdom.
Later, Shri Hari invited Raghavji and Valji to the grand Mahavishnuyag in Dabhan. Both brothers traveled to Dabhan and were blessed by beholding Shri Hari seated upon the sacrificial altar. Immensely pleased with their devotion, Shri Hari took off two gold rings (vedh) from His own hands and gifted one to each brother. Blessed with Shri Hari&rsquo;s divine grace, both brothers returned to Dhoraji with hearts full of devotion.
From &lsquo;Shri Hari Leelamrutam&rsquo;&hellip; 🙏
