Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The Wrestlers of Bhuj and Shriji Maharaj&rsquo;s Divine Majesty Once, Shriji Maharaj was resting upon a wooden cot at the home of carpenter Hirjibhai in Bhujnagar. At that time, Jethi Gangaram and five to six other prominent wrestlers were present. They gathered together and began massaging Shriji Maharaj&rsquo;s lotus feet and body.
Shriji Maharaj playfully remarked, &ldquo;Does the local Darbar not provide you sufficient rations and nutritious diet? And if he does, do you eat it heartily or not?&rdquo;
The wrestlers replied, &ldquo;Maharaj! The Darbar generously provides ample rations, and we eat lavishly to our heart&rsquo;s content.&rdquo;
Shriji Maharaj challenged them with a smile, &ldquo;If you eat so well, where has all your strength gone? Apply some real force and massage My feet!&rdquo;
Thereupon, all six wrestlers joined forces and began massaging Maharaj&rsquo;s lotus feet with all their might. Straining with all their strength, they broke into heavy sweats, their clothes became drenched, and they were thoroughly exhausted; yet Maharaj felt not the slightest pressure and simply smiled serene and untroubled.
Realizing His divine transcendence, all the wrestlers folded their hands in awe and proclaimed, &ldquo;O Maharaj! You are Bhagwan Pratyaksh Purushottam Narayan Himself! Where is Your infinite majesty, and where is our petty mortal strength? Today You have shown boundless mercy by granting us this extraordinary divine revelation. As long as we live, we shall cherish the memory of this divine lila. O Lord, please protect and assist us at the time of our death!&rdquo;
Shriji Maharaj blessed them, &ldquo;You belong to Us; We shall protect you in every conceivable manner.&rdquo; In this way, while residing in Bhujnagar, Shriji Maharaj revealed His multifarious divine glory to the devotees and bathed daily in the sacred waters of Hamirsar lake.
One day, Shriji Maharaj imparted the sacred technique of meditating upon God to carpenter Sundarjibhai. As Shriji Maharaj instructed, Sundarjibhai began to practice meditation. He retreated to his north-facing room, purified himself by washing his hands and feet, sat upon a sanctified mat facing north, and entered meditation.
At that time, Shriji Maharaj was seated outside in the courtyard. Five solid walls separated Shriji Maharaj from Sundarjibhai. Yet, the moment Sundarjibhai entered meditation, he clearly beheld the divine darshan of Shriji Maharaj through all five intervening walls!
Sundarjibhai reflected within himself, &ldquo;I am neither asleep nor dreaming. But when I sat beside Maharaj earlier, other devotees were present, but Mehta Ganpatram was not there; now in my meditation, I see Ganpatram sitting there wrapped in a woolen shawl. Let me step outside to Shriji Maharaj; if Ganpatram is indeed present, it will confirm that when one meditates upon Maharaj in this manner, no physical obstacle can obstruct one&rsquo;s spiritual vision.&rdquo;
Sundarjibhai walked out into the courtyard and prostrated at Shriji Maharaj&rsquo;s feet. Looking at Sundarjibhai, Shriji Maharaj smiled warmly and asked, &ldquo;How is it with you?&rdquo;
Sundarjibhai submitted with folded hands, &ldquo;O Maharaj! Just as a man possessing the wish-fulfilling gem (Chintamani) obtains whatever he desires, all the power and divinity within the Chintamani and the wish-fulfilling tree (Kalpavriksha) are bestowed by God alone. That very Supreme God has manifested directly before us, granting us continuous darshan! You teach us the true way of worshipping God and meditating upon Him, and You fulfill all our inner desires; what wonder is there in this? O Maharaj! Please grant us darshan whenever we remember You, and bless me that the unalloyed love I feel for You today may remain eternal!&rdquo;
Shriji Maharaj bestowed the boon, &ldquo;It shall remain so.&rdquo;
A few days later, Shriji Maharaj announced, &ldquo;We now intend to proceed to Mankuva.&rdquo; Hearing of Maharaj&rsquo;s departure, Sundarjibhai was overcome with the sorrow of impending separation and developed a high fever. Hirjibhai informed Maharaj, &ldquo;O Maharaj! Sundarjibhai has developed a severe fever upon hearing that You are leaving for Mankuva.&rdquo;
Shriji Maharaj smiled and said, &ldquo;Go and tell Sundarjibhai that Maharaj will not go to Mankuva.&rdquo; The moment Hirjibhai delivered this message, Sundarjibhai&rsquo;s fever vanished completely! Whenever Maharaj mentioned leaving, Sundarjibhai would be gripped by fever. In this manner, displaying His divine power and affection, Shri Hari showered boundless bliss upon His devotees and resided in Bhuj for two full months before departing for Mankuva.
