Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The Fakir of Bhachau and the Divine Form of Ramchandraji Once, Shri Hari graced the village of Bhachau in Kutch and stayed at the residence of devotee Shah Vagha. After partaking of a lovingly prepared thal at his home, Maharaj visited the local Darbar to bestow spiritual liberation upon earnest seekers.
Some thoughtful seekers of the village gathered and discussed among themselves, &ldquo;This Swaminarayan, who is revered as a Jivanmukta, is currently residing at the Darbar. Let us all go to listen to His spiritual discourses and pose some questions. He is said to be God, so let us also seek a divine miracle (parcho); if He is truly God, it will become evident. Moreover, our village fakir is very wise and experienced; let us take him along.&rdquo;
Taking the fakir with them, the villagers gathered at the Darbar. Offering coconuts before Shri Hari and bowing reverently, they sat facing Him. Village Patel Khima petitioned, &ldquo;O Maharaj! We have come to hear spiritual discourse, so please impart divine wisdom to us.&rdquo;
Shriji Maharaj said to Mayaram Bhatt, &ldquo;Bhattji, please speak to them.&rdquo;
The villagers said, &ldquo;We have listened to Bhattji&rsquo;s discourses our entire lives; we have come specifically to hear the divine words from Maharaj&rsquo;s own lips. Therefore, please speak to us Yourself.&rdquo;
Thereupon, Shriji Maharaj delivered an extensive, sublime discourse elucidating devotion, knowledge, and the paramount importance of worshipping God. Afterwards, the villagers said, &ldquo;O Maharaj! You induce divine trance (samadhi); we have heard of this from others and have come to witness samadhi firsthand. Please grant us samadhi.&rdquo;
Hearing this, Maharaj addressed Jeram Bhagat (who later became Sadguru Nirlobhanand Swami, but was then a householder clad in white garments): &ldquo;Jeram Bhagat, sit in solitude and meditate, and you will enter samadhi.&rdquo;
Jeram Bhagat sat in a quiet corner to meditate. After a while, Shriji Maharaj asked, &ldquo;What did you behold in your meditation?&rdquo;
Jeram Bhagat answered candidly, &ldquo;Two women were quarreling nearby; my mind drifted toward their dispute, so I saw nothing.&rdquo;
Shri Hari smiled and remarked, &ldquo;You are mixing pebbles with khichdi while eating; how then can you relish the sweet taste of khichdi?&rdquo;
Jeram Bhagat submitted, &ldquo;O Maharaj! You are the Lord of lords. We have come to You precisely so that You may separate the pebbles from our khichdi; please show us the means by which they may be separated.&rdquo;
Maharaj asked, &ldquo;Which deity is the object of your personal worship (upasana)?&rdquo;
The devotee replied, &ldquo;We worship Lord Ramchandraji.&rdquo;
Maharaj asked, &ldquo;Have you ever seen the murti of Ramchandraji? Behold, We shall show you Lord Ramchandraji; He was exactly like this; meditate upon this form.&rdquo;
Saying this, Shriji Maharaj revealed all His divine limbs: first displaying His lotus feet adorned with the sixteen sacred emblems and vertical lines (urdhva rekha), saying: &ldquo;Lord Ramchandraji&rsquo;s lotus feet, endowed with sixteen marks, were exactly like these. Behold, His calves, knees, and thighs were identical to these; His abdomen and broad chest were identical; and His lotus face, eyes, nose, and head were exactly like these. Lord Ramchandraji&rsquo;s divine form was identical to this. Enshrine these limbs within your heart and meditate upon them.&rdquo;
Hearing this, Jeram Bhagat said, &ldquo;O Maharaj! For those who meditate as You have instructed, this path becomes exceedingly simple,&rdquo; and he prostrated at His lotus feet.
Meanwhile, the villagers turned to the fakir who had accompanied them and asked, &ldquo;What have you concluded?&rdquo;
The fakir replied in sheer astonishment, &ldquo;Listen, my friends! Whenever I visit our revered Pirs, Fakirs, or Auliyas, if I tap my wooden staff ever so lightly on the ground, it produces a deafening crack like a gunshot! But before &lsquo;Swaminarayan&rsquo;, I struck my staff three times upon the earth with all my strength, yet it did not emit the slightest sound! Swaminarayan is Hindu and you are Hindu; believe it or not, my staff fell utterly mute before Swaminarayan! Seeing this, I am filled with profound wonder. Allah whispers to my heart: &lsquo;Swaminarayan is truly Khuda (God)!&rsquo; He has granted me a direct miracle!&rdquo;
Shortly thereafter, all the villagers bowed and returned home. Shri Hari then summoned Akhandanand Swami and instructed him, &ldquo;There are numerous sincere spiritual seekers in this village, and Satsang will flourish here. Therefore, remain here for ten days and impart spiritual wisdom to all. We must proceed to Bhuj today.&rdquo;
Shriji Maharaj departed for Bhuj, while Akhandanand Swami remained in Bhachau. All those who had questioned Maharaj and requested samadhi embraced Satsang under Swami&rsquo;s spiritual guidance.
Later, those devotees expressed to Akhandanand Swami, &ldquo;Out of supreme compassion, Shriji Maharaj revealed His holy feet with sixteen marks and all His divine limbs, telling us that Ramchandraji&rsquo;s form was like this; but our limited intellect could not grasp the divine secret at that time. Now, listening to your discourses, we have realized the truth: Shriji Maharaj Himself is the Supreme Source of Lord Ramchandraji, Shri Krishna, and all divine incarnations! He mercifully stationed you here, rescuing us from the jaws of Kal and death. Otherwise, we would have drifted helplessly in the worldly ocean, wasted this precious human birth, and suffered endlessly through the cycle of 8.4 million life forms. Today our eternal salvation is assured, and it is entirely by the supreme grace of Shriji Maharaj!&rdquo;
