Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Counsel to Kathi Devotees to Live Like King Janak, the Pain of Separation, and Constant Darshan In Gadhada, many Kathi chieftains and Garasiya devotees from distant villages were lingering in the sublime presence of Shreeji Maharaj, completely absorbed in the bliss of His company. One day, Shreehari lovingly guided them regarding their worldly duties: &ldquo;All Kathi and Garasiya devotees who have arrived from other villages should now return to their homes, manage their family responsibilities, and faithfully obey My commands. Reside in the world unattached, just as King Janak lived as a detached Videhi soul!&rdquo;
Hearing the command to depart, tears welled up in the eyes of the loving devotees. With trembling hands and choking voices, they pleaded: &ldquo;O Lord! When our eyes behold Your radiant countenance, our souls cannot bear even the momentary separation caused by the blinking of our eyelids! How then could we possibly endure living far away in distant villages? Pray keep us eternally before Your holy presence!&rdquo;
Deeply moved by their profound love and pangs of separation (virah), compassionate Shreehari comforted them with a magnificent benediction: &ldquo;Meditate upon Me constantly within your hearts! My divine form shall remain uninterruptedly visible before your inner vision, and you shall never experience separation from Me!&rdquo;
Uplifted and consoled by this divine promise, the devotees peacefully returned to their homes, carrying the Lord&rsquo;s living presence within their hearts.
