Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Sadguru Bhayatmanand Swami and Gunatitanand Swami (The Mystery of Upasana) Once, Sadguru Gunatitanand Swami was returning from Vadtal to Junagadh. On the way lay the village of Vagad. On the outskirts of Vagad, near the boundary of Aniyali village, lived Sadguru Bhayatmanand Swami. At that time, Bhayatmanand Swami had reached the venerable age of 116 years. Due to his advanced physical age, only the local water of Vagad suited his health, which is why he resided there. Gurudev Gunatitanand Swami came specifically to visit Bhai Swami. Gunatitanand Swami would never make such a visit without a profound spiritual purpose. The moment Swami set foot in his dwelling, Bhayatmanand Swami sat up and embraced him with deep affection. Bhayatmanand Swami exclaimed, &ldquo;Ohoho! Welcome, Swami! Please be seated. Swami, I was just contemplating that I have reached 116 years of age. I spent 30 glorious years in the personal company of Maharaj, and for the past 30 years I have endured separation (viyog) from Shriji Maharaj. In my extreme old age, even a new set of teeth has grown! Yet, Swami, why has Maharaj not come to escort me to His divine Abode? Swami, what flaw or shortcoming (kasar) remains in me? Once, carrying this very question, I traveled to Junagadh to see you, but you had departed on a spiritual tour of the Sorath region. You did not return for many days, and the water of Junagadh did not agree with my health. The water I had brought along was exhausted, so I had to return here. But today, Shriji Maharaj Himself has sent you to me. Please tell me, what shortcoming remains in me?&rdquo;
Gunatitanand Swami replied, &ldquo;Swami, Maharaj has accepted you as His own &lsquo;brother&rsquo; (Bhai); what other shortcoming could there possibly be in your life? There is none at all! However, there is a minor deficiency solely in your understanding of Upasana (the supreme divine status of Bhagwan Swaminarayan). Eradicate that singular flaw, and Shriji Maharaj will immediately escort you to His eternal Abode. Swami, Maharaj holds immense love for you. It is only to ensure that you never have to take another birth in this world that He has kept you here until now.&rdquo;
Bhayatmanand Swami asked, &ldquo;O Swami! What deficiency could there be in my Upasana?&rdquo; Gunatitanand Swami explained, &ldquo;Listen, Swami. Whenever the discourse turned to Upasana in spiritual gatherings, you would brush it aside saying, &lsquo;Oh, leave all that! Why bother weighing one measure against two (comparing ser and basher)?&rsquo; Because you dismissed the discussion in this manner, no one ever spoke further.&rdquo;
Bhayatmanand Swami admitted, &ldquo;Yes, Swami, that is true. Even now, I have believed that the previous incarnations (avatars) and this King of Kings Shriji Maharaj are one and the same. Swami, please explain to me how I should truly understand this.&rdquo;
Gunatitanand Swami then had the Vachanamruts regarding Upasana brought out and read one by one, elucidating the profound mystery of Upasana. Swami then narrated: &ldquo;Bhayatmanand Swami, listen! When Vyapkanand Swami had not yet attained firm conviction in Maharaj’s supreme status (Sarvopari-panu), Shri Hari drew him into samadhi and sent him to Akshardham. In Akshardham, Vyapkanand Swami worshipped Maharaj. Then a desire arose in Swami&rsquo;s mind to worship all the infinite liberated souls (muktas) seated there simultaneously. But he wondered how he could perform such a simultaneous worship (ek-kalavachhinna puja). Maharaj instructed him, &lsquo;Swami, invoke the name of each avatar one by one and make a resolve that if any among them is the supreme cause of all incarnations (Sarvavatari), may you assume countless forms and worship all muktas simultaneously.&rsquo; Vyapkanand Swami made that resolve, yet he could not assume multiple forms. Then Maharaj said, &lsquo;Swami, now take Our name and make a resolve: &ldquo;If this Sahajanand Swami is the supreme Sarvavatari Purushottam Narayan, may I assume infinite forms and perform simultaneous worship of all.&rdquo;&rsquo; The moment Vyapkanand Swami made this resolve, he instantly manifested into infinite forms and worshipped Maharaj along with all the muktas at the same moment. Atmanand Swami, surely you know of this episode?&rdquo; Bhayatmanand Swami replied, &ldquo;Yes, Swami, I know of it.&rdquo; Gunatitanand Swami continued, &ldquo;In the village of Nagadka, right before the eyes of Vyapkanand Swami, the twenty-four avatars manifested from Maharaj&rsquo;s divine murti and merged back into Maharaj’s murti; you were present there as well. Do you remember that incident?&rdquo;
Bhayatmanand Swami affirmed, &ldquo;Yes, Swami, I remember it well.&rdquo; Gunatitanand Swami further said, &ldquo;Swami, you also know the incident of Parvatbhai, don&rsquo;t you? Parvatbhai once wondered in his mind how God had assumed the Nrusimha avatar. Immediately, the twenty-four avatars manifested before him and then merged back into Maharaj’s divine murti.&rdquo; Bhayatmanand Swami said, &ldquo;Yes, Swami, I know that divine account as well.&rdquo;
Gunatitanand Swami then explained the supreme truth: &ldquo;Swami, what is the true meaning behind all these divine occurrences? Avatars emerge from the Avatari and merge back into the Avatari. All avatars emanate from Shriji Maharaj, and the supreme Avatari who encompasses all avatars is Sahajanand Swami Himself—the Supreme Purushottam Narayan! Firmly instill this profound understanding within your heart, and Shriji Maharaj will immediately take you to His eternal Abode.&rdquo; In this manner, Gunatitanand Swami unveiled the esoteric truth of Upasana to Bhayatmanand Swami. Before departing, Gunatitanand Swami said to the exalted devotee Shivlal Sheth, &ldquo;Shivlal, now Maharaj will soon escort Swami to the divine Abode.&rdquo;
On the auspicious day of Jeth Vadi Chhath, Samvat 1916, Shriji Maharaj took Sadguru Bhayatmanand Swami to His eternal Akshardham.
