Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Govind Merai of Gadhdaka: Unmatched Spiritual Conviction, Stitched Clothes, and Pot Water In the village of Gadhdaka lived Govind Merai, a tailor and an exceptionally staunch devotee of Bhagwan Swaminarayan. Earning a modest living through his tailoring work, he lived a life of spotless integrity. Ever since he accepted the Swaminarayan faith, skeptical villagers frequently mocked and ridiculed him.
One day, some village skeptics taunted him, saying, &ldquo;Hey Govind! You spend day and night chanting &lsquo;Swaminarayan&hellip; Swaminarayan&hellip;&rsquo; Do you really think you have secured your salvation? Why are you wasting your time?&rdquo;
Hearing these mocking remarks, righteous pride and divine conviction surged through Govind Merai&rsquo;s soul. He retorted boldly with towering spiritual authority: &ldquo;Brothers! Why speak of my salvation alone? Whoever wears the garments stitched by my hands and whoever drinks a sip of water from the clay pot in my house—Bhagwan Swaminarayan will liberate them as well! What doubt could there possibly be regarding my own liberation?&rdquo;
Witnessing his unshakable conviction in the omnipotent grace of the Supreme Lord, the skeptics were completely silenced and retreated in embarrassment.
No fear can touch the soul anchored in Shreehari&rsquo;s infinite glory! Men and women abide fearless, their minds undisturbed by worldly dread. While living in the body they know no sorrow, and after death they ascend to the eternal Abode; Beholding the majesty of their Lord, they revel in boundless inner bliss!
