Meanwhile, back in Rajpur, the elderly mother of devotee Vajaji had remained unaware of Shreehari’s visit and missed His divine darshan. Learning that the Lord had departed, she was struck with unbearable grief: &ldquo;The Supreme Lord Himself came to our village, yet I missed His darshan; what purpose does this mortal life serve now?&rdquo; Weeping inconsolably, the sheer agony of separation caused her to collapse critically ill. She pleaded with her son Vajaji, &ldquo;Go this instant and bring Shreehari back from wherever He is, or my breath will forsake my body!&rdquo; Vajaji comforted her, &ldquo;Mother, the Lord is omniscient; if our devotion is sincere, He will return unbidden this very hour!&rdquo;
Resting in Irana, omniscient Shreehari perceived the heartfelt lament of the devout mother and sprang up instantly! Instructing Mulji Brahmachari and the sadhus to follow at their own pace, Shreehari mounted His swift Rozo stallion and galloped back toward Rajpur like lightning. In moments, He vaulted into Vajaji’s courtyard, rushed to the ailing mother’s cot, and called out tenderly: &ldquo;Look, mother! You remembered Us with such longing, and here We are before you!&rdquo;
Beholding Shreehari’s radiant smiling face, vitality surged through the elderly woman’s frail body! Her illness and despair dissolved in an instant. Rising from her cot with renewed youthfulness, she performed aarti, applied sandalwood-kumkum to Shreehari&rsquo;s forehead, and prostrated in gratitude. Soon after, the sadhus arrived, and Vajaji hosted the entire holy entourage for dinner and an overnight stay. Thus, bound by unalloyed devotion, Shreehari rushed back to comfort His devotee.
