Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Divine Leela beneath the Neem Tree in Gadhpur and the Narrative of Oghadji Once, Shri Hari was seated upon a cot beneath the sacred neem tree in the courtyard of Dada Khachar in Gadhpur. An assembly of revered saints, devotees, and parshads was seated before Him in deep devotion. Sura Khachar, Shri Hari’s beloved companion, was sitting right beside the cot. At that time, Shri Hari affectionately turned to Sura Khachar and said, &ldquo;Sura Bapu! Please narrate to Us the narrative (akhyan) of Oghadji of your village, which you have composed!&rdquo;
Without hesitation, Sura Bapu tuned into his resonant, deep voice and sang the sacred story and devotional kirtans celebrating Oghadji. Shri Hari was immensely pleased upon hearing this extraordinary narrative.
At that divine moment, countless liberated souls (muktas) and celestial deities arrived via the skies in their heavenly chariots (vimanas) to behold Shri Hari’s divine darshan and listen to this sacred discourse. Shri Hari bestowed a benevolent boon upon Sura Bapu: &ldquo;Whoever sings or listens with devotion to this narrative of Oghadji composed by you shall attain the supreme abode (Param Pad / Akshardham), and Shri Hari shall alleviate all their distress.&rdquo;
Thus, by presiding beneath the sacred neem tree that day, Shri Hari bestowed boundless divine bliss upon all the devotees and deepened the spirit of pure devotion in the Satsang fellowship.
From Shri Hari Charitra Chintamani&hellip; 🙏
