Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The Double Arch of Vadtal Mandir and Brahmanand Swami&rsquo;s Architectural Mastery By the divine command of Shri Hari, Sadguru Brahmanand Swami was overseeing the construction of the grand Vadtal Mandir. The temple construction was progressing in full swing. One day, while inspecting the pillars, arches, and ornamental porticos (rupchoki) of the temple, Swami arrived at the portico of the main entrance. Brahmanand Swami summoned the sculptors and artisans, instructing them, &ldquo;Carvings adorn all the arches, but since this is the main gateway, we should sculpt a double arch with intricate carvings in this portico.&rdquo;
The artisans humbly submitted, &ldquo;Swami, across all the grand Hindu temples, only a single arch is carved at the main entrances. We have never seen a double arch anywhere, and that is why we have carved a single arch here as well.&rdquo;
Brahmanand Swami smiled and asked, &ldquo;Have you studied the ancient classical scriptures of temple architecture, such as Rajvallabh and Prasadmandan?&rdquo;
The artisans looked at Swami in astonishment and replied, &ldquo;Swami, we have never studied such sacred scriptures! We simply observe older temples and execute our carving and stonework accordingly.&rdquo;
Upon hearing this, Swami immediately called for paper and, with his own hands, sketched a precise architectural drawing of the double arch for the main entrance portico. Instructing them to carve the arch according to the classical principles of shilpa shastra, Swami said, &ldquo;Now, craft your intricate carvings upon this double arch and the ornamental embellishments of its pillars. Prepare the drawings, cut the stencils, and begin carving! Even though you have never crafted such work before, if you follow this blueprint drawn by me, by the divine grace and power of Bhagwan Shri Hari, you will master it effortlessly—this is my blessing upon you.&rdquo;
All the artisans touched Swami&rsquo;s lotus feet with deep reverence and resolved to carve the double arch.
Within a few days, blessed by Swami&rsquo;s grace, the sculptors finished carving the magnificent double arch and installed it at the main entrance portico. It looked extraordinarily beautiful and majestic. Sadguru Brahmanand Swami was immensely pleased with all the artisans and showered them with heartfelt divine blessings.
Later, when Vairagyamurti Sadguru Shri Nishkulanand Swami was supervising the construction of the temple of Shri Madanmohanji Maharaj in Dholera, he came to Vadtal, drew the blueprint of this unique arch, and had the artisans construct an identical double arch at the main entrance of Dholera Mandir. To this day, these splendid arches stand in the mandirs of Vadtal and Dholera, bearing eternal testimony to the unparalleled architectural genius and divine vision of Sadguru Brahmanand Swami and Sadguru Nishkulanand Swami.
