Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Kunvarji Patel of Ingorala and the Teachings of Bhai Swami Sadguru Bhayatmanand Swami (fondly known as &lsquo;Bhai Swami&rsquo;) resided mostly in the village of Vagad. On one occasion, Patel Kunvarji Jagani of Ingorala village was traveling on administrative business for the Vadodara princely state and planned to halt at Vagad along the way. Ahead of his visit, Kothari Bhaktivallabh Swami sent a letter from Gadhada to Bhai Swami stating, &ldquo;Kunvarji Jagani is a devoted and noble satsangi; kindly ensure he is looked after well and extend warm hospitality to him.&rdquo; When he arrived, the devotees at Vagad graciously accommodated Kunvarjibhai in the mandir premises and lovingly served him sanctified meals.
However, Kunvarji Patel had a deep habit of smoking the hookah. While sitting in the spiritual assembly alongside Swami, he sent his personal attendant, a barber, to fetch acacia bark or burning coals to light the hookah. The attendant went to the local devotees asking for the materials. Hearing this request, the devotees remarked among themselves, &ldquo;From Gadhada, Kothari Swami wrote that he is an exemplary devotee deserving great hospitality, yet he turns out to be an incorrigible hookah addict! Can a true devotee of God ever remain bonded to a hookah?&rdquo;
Kunvarji Jagani overheard these words, and a wave of introspection swept over him. He thought to himself, &ldquo;In his letter, Kothari Swami praised me so generously, yet this wretched hookah has brought me shame and humiliation before everyone!&rdquo; Determined, he immediately stood up, walked to the stone steps of the mandir, smashed the hookah to pieces, and retired to his room.
Later that night, as Kunvarji Patel lay resting in his quarters at the mandir, his attendant barber was pressing and massaging his legs. Around midnight, Bhai Swami woke up and noticed the attendant massaging his legs. The next morning, Bhai Swami called Kunvarji Patel to his side and asked, &ldquo;What is the purpose of having your legs massaged like this?&rdquo;
Kunvarji Patel replied sheepishly, &ldquo;Swami, unless the barber massages my legs, sleep eludes me.&rdquo;
Bhai Swami then imparted profound wisdom, saying, &ldquo;If tomorrow circumstances change, times turn harsh, and there is no one left to massage your legs, how will you ever sleep? Have you ever contemplated that? A devotee should remain self-reliant and free from reliance on pampering luxuries.&rdquo;
Kunvarji Jagani instantly understood the deep spiritual truth in Swami&rsquo;s guidance. That very moment, he paid the barber his full wages along with traveling expenses and sent him back home. From that day onward, he became completely free of all addictions—renouncing the hookah forever—and completely abandoned luxurious dependencies like foot massages for the rest of his life. Through the divine blessings and spiritual guidance of Bhai Swami, he attained true inner peace, self-reliance, and enduring happiness.
From the spiritual discourses of Sadguru Shri Aksharanand Swami&hellip; 🙏
