Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Jivanbhai of Maliya and Shriji Maharaj&rsquo;s Divine Protection In the village of Maliya, a devout devotee named Thakkar Jivanbhai fell grievously ill. He developed a severe and agonizing affliction known as ratvo (an acute, painful septic abscess or carbuncle) on his neck, causing him unbearable torment day and night. Around that time, Sadguru Mahapurushdasji Swami arrived in Maliya during his Satsang spiritual tour (vicharan) and stayed at the village mandir. When someone informed Swami about Jivanbhai’s worsening condition, the compassionate sadhu promptly visited his home to inquire after his wellbeing.
Standing beside Jivanbhai’s bedside, Swami led the assembled sadhus and devotees in singing the divine chanting (dhun) of the Swaminarayan Mahamantra. Jivanbhai’s father-in-law was present at the scene and remarked somewhat skeptically, &ldquo;Your Guru Ramanand Swami possessed such divine power that he would cure serious ailments with just a pinch of sacred ash (rakh)! Why do you not demonstrate a similar miracle?&rdquo; Hearing this, Mahapurushdas Swami replied with serene conviction, &ldquo;We too can cure Jivanbhai by tomorrow morning in that very manner, provided you immediately discard the enchanted superstitious threads and charms you have tied around his neck!&rdquo; At the urging of other family members, the father-in-law relented and agreed to remove those occult charms.
Swami then returned to the mandir with his assembly of sadhus. Placing all the sadhus before the sacred murti of Thakorji, Swami instructed each to turn twenty-five rosaries (malas), while he fervently prayed to Shriji Maharaj: &ldquo;O merciful Lord! Please alleviate Jivanbhai&rsquo;s agonizing pain from this ratvo and restore him to sound health.&rdquo;
Moved by the sincere plea of His holy sadhu, the Supreme Lord Shriji Maharaj arrived in the middle of the night at Jivanbhai’s home to bestow divine darshan and heal him. However, observing that other superstitious threads were still tied around Jivanbhai&rsquo;s neck by his father-in-law, Shri Hari refrained from appearing directly to him and instead granted His divine darshan to Jivanbhai’s devoted wife. Beholding the luminous form of Shri Hari in her home at midnight, she was overwhelmed with immense joy and reverence. Shri Hari gently told her, &ldquo;We came here in response to Mahapurushdas Swami’s heartfelt prayer to grant darshan to your husband and cure his illness; yet seeing that your father has tied superstitious threads around Jivanbhai’s neck, We are returning! Convey this message to them: the moment they untie and discard all those superstitious threads in the morning, the abscess will rupture and drain, and he will be completely relieved of all suffering.&rdquo;
At dawn, Jivanbhai’s wife recounted the divine vision and message of Shri Hari to the entire family. Realizing their mistake, they immediately removed and discarded all superstitious threads from his neck. Just as Shri Hari had promised, the painful abscess burst open and drained naturally, the unbearable torment ceased instantly, and Jivanbhai was restored to full health. In this manner, Shriji Maharaj protected His devotee from a fatal illness while eradicating superstition and blind faith, establishing unswerving devotion solely in the Almighty.
From Shri Haricharitramrut Chintamani&hellip; 🙏
