Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The Steadfast Faith of Joban Pagi and Shivo Gadhvi Once, Shri Hari was addressing an assembly of saints and devotees on the spiritual virtue of resolute conviction and unwavering faith (Nishtha no ang). On that occasion, He narrated two extraordinary incidents&hellip;
The First Incident: Once, Joban Pagi was traveling on foot from Vadtal to Gadhada accompanied by his two daughters to have divine darshan. Walking along their way, they reached Dholera, had darshan of the deity, and proceeded toward the village of Polarpur. As noon approached, they washed their hands and faces by the bank of a village pond and sat down to eat lunch. They ate the dhebra, chillies, jaggery, and yogurt they had brought along, and then rested for a while in the cool shade of a tree.
At that time, a group of ten to twelve merchants (Vaniyas) passed by. Seeing Joban Pagi, they asked, &ldquo;You appear to be wayfarers; where do you reside?&rdquo; Joban Pagi replied, &ldquo;We belong to Gujarat and are traveling to the village of Gadhada in Kathiyawad.&rdquo; Hearing this, one of the merchants remarked, &ldquo;In Gujarat, there is one known as Joban of Vadtal, who was once a notorious, ruthless bandit, but has now become a follower of Swaminarayan. We hear that Swaminarayan ran off with his two daughters—is that true?&rdquo;
Joban Pagi replied with calm conviction, &ldquo;Did He take away only two, or even more? In His Krishna incarnation, my Beloved Lord accepted 16,108 queens. As long as He does up to that number, I shall recognize Him as none other than Bhagwan Shri Krishna! And if He does twice or thrice that number, my understanding of His supreme glory (mahatmya) will only double or triple!&rdquo;
The merchants did not know that they were addressing Joban Pagi himself, but hearing such unshakeable faith and fearless conviction, they were struck dumb with awe.
Joban Pagi then stated, &ldquo;Look here! The Joban of Vadtal you are speaking about is myself, and these two daughters of mine are right here with me! My Ishtadev Bhagwan Shri Swaminarayan has not run away with my daughters; rather, you should protect your own mothers, sisters, and daughters, for many hypocritical impostors and mendicants wander about in society who might deceive them, leaving you to weep bitter tears later!&rdquo;
Shri Hari then related the second incident of unwavering conviction in the assembly on that very day&hellip;
The Second Incident: Once, in the village of Vaso, the devotee Shivo Gadhvi and Kasiyoji were sitting together in Ramdas&rsquo;s court. At that moment, Shivo Gadhvi stood up. Kasiyoji asked, &ldquo;Gadhvi, why are you standing up to leave?&rdquo; Shivo Gadhvi replied, &ldquo;My Ishtadev Bhagwan Swaminarayan has currently graced Vadtal, and I must go to have His darshan.&rdquo;
Hearing this, Kasiyoji taunted with malice, &ldquo;Gadhvi, what royal robe of honor (shirpav) is He going to bestow upon you that you keep running after Him time and again?&rdquo;
Shivo Gadhvi replied with unyielding faith, &ldquo;Even if He does not tie a royal robe of honor upon me, He is millions and billions of times greater than you! You can only offer me transient worldly possessions of this mortal realm, whereas He will sever the cycle of birth and death and grant me the eternal abode of Akshardham! He is my Supreme Lord, and that is why I am going.&rdquo;
Proclaiming this powerful declaration of faith, Shivo Gadhvi left the court and went straight to Vadtal, where he had darshan of Shriji Maharaj and sat down in the assembly.
Recounting that moment, Maharaj said, &ldquo;At that time, We were wearing a cotton-padded surval (trousers), an expensive satin (atalas) jamo (long robe), and had tied a moliyu (turban) on Our head and draped a shelu (shawl). Knowing Shivo Gadhvi&rsquo;s resolute devotion through Our divine omniscience, We called him close, dressed him in all those very clothes of Ours, and blessed him, saying: &lsquo;Go, wearing these very garments, and tell Kasiyoji that my Bhagwan, knowing everything through His omniscience, has sent me back specifically to show and tell you!&rsquo;&rdquo;
Saying this, Maharaj sent Shivo Gadhvi back to Vaso village.
Among the sacred prasadi garments gifted to the great devotee Shivo Gadhvi, the jamo and surval are preserved and can be viewed for darshan even today.
From the sacred discourses of Sadguru Shri Adbhutanand Swami&hellip; 🙏
