Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The True Nature of Divine Love: Adbhutanand Swami&rsquo;s Yearning for Darshan Once, Lord Swaminarayan was presiding over an assembly beneath the cool shade of the holy neem tree in the Darbargadh of Gadhpur. During the discourse, the Kathi chieftains inquired out of heartfelt curiosity: &ldquo;O Maharaj! What is the true essence and nature of pure divine love (het)?&rdquo;
Smiling serenely, the omniscient Lord remarked: &ldquo;Dear Darbars, Sadguru Muktanand Swami will arrive here in two days; he will explain and demonstrate to you what genuine divine love truly looks like.&rdquo;
At the same time, Sadguru Adbhutanand Swami was engaged in spiritual travels across distant regions. Six long months had elapsed without beholding the divine form of Shreeji Maharaj, and an overwhelming craving for His darshan engulfed Swami&rsquo;s heart. With the auspicious festival of Sharad Purnima (Manekthari Punam) fast approaching, he hastened towards Gadhada. However, upon reaching the Dodiya crossroads, a severe and agonizing affliction of guinea-worm (vaalo) broke out in his foot. The pain was excruciating, making it virtually impossible to take a single step. He agonized inwardly: &ldquo;In this condition, how will I ever reach Gadhpur?&rdquo;
Miraculously, at that very crossroads, Sadguru Muktanand Swami arrived with his traveling party of sadhus. Overjoyed at meeting each other, Muktanand Swami noticed Adbhutanand Swami&rsquo;s distress and proposed lovingly: &ldquo;Swami, you are enduring unbearable pain. Let us send the junior ascetics ahead to Gadhpur while you and I stay right here. I will nurse and serve you until the affliction subsides; then we shall travel.&rdquo;
Hearing this, Adbhutanand Swami replied with tears of longing: &ldquo;Swami! My soul cannot bear to live another day without the divine darshan of Shreeji Maharaj. I implore you to fetch me a simple wooden walking staff; leaning upon it, I shall limp along slowly in your holy company.&rdquo;
Early the following morning, the party set out. Bearing the intense throbbing in his foot, Adbhutanand Swami limped and hobbled with the staff across thirty-two arduous kilometers until they reached the village of Kundal. Junior ascetics had arrived ahead to inform the noble devotee Raibai Maa, who received the revered elders with immense reverence, performed their puja, fed them fresh consecrated laddus, and hosted them graciously in her estate.
The next day, despite Raibai&rsquo;s affectionate pleas to rest, the ascetics insisted on reaching Gadhada. Recognizing their yearning, Raibai harnessed a bullock cart, lined it with soft quilts, and arranged for the elderly sadhus to be conveyed in comfort.
Meanwhile in Gadhpur, Shreeji Maharaj intuitively sensed their arrival. Mounting His beloved mare, Manki, He rode out to welcome them, intercepting the cart about two miles outside the town boundary. Commanding the saints to remain seated, Maharaj rode Manki in five reverent clockwise circumambulations around the humble bullock cart! Dismounting, He prostrated before the holy saints with full dandvat pranam and embraced them tightly in His arms. In that divine embrace, Adbhutanand Swami felt every trace of physical agony vanish, replaced by streams of ecstatic tears. Leading the grand procession on Manki with the saints&rsquo; cart following behind, Maharaj orchestrated a jubilant reception into the Darbargadh, personally serving them a delicious devotional feast.
Later that afternoon, when the assembly convened beneath the neem tree, Maharaj turned to the chieftains: &ldquo;Now Muktanand Swami will explain to you the true meaning of divine love.&rdquo;
Sadguru Muktanand Swami revealed with deep emotion: &ldquo;Behold, Darbars! Adbhutanand Swami is the living personification of supreme divine affection. Despite an agonizing guinea-worm wound that crippled his leg, his burning thirst for Shreeji Maharaj&rsquo;s darshan drove him to limp thirty-two grueling kilometers upon a wooden stick, refusing to halt even when begged to rest. Forgetting bodily existence entirely out of supreme love for the beloved Lord is the true essence of divine love!&rdquo;
