Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The Mop of Muli Doshi in Ghandla and the Compassion of Muktanand Swami Once, Sadguru Muktanand Swami was touring the region of Mahuva along with his traveling party of sadhus. Arriving at the village of Ghandla, Swami established camp beneath the shade of a large tree on the riverbank. Junior ascetics ventured into the village streets for alms (bhikshavritti) so that whatever grain was received could be cooked, offered to Thakorji, and partaken as holy prasadam.
The sadhus entered a residential courtyard and chanted the customary greeting: &ldquo;Jai Sachidanand Prabho! Narayan Hare!&rdquo; Hearing this, the elderly mistress of the home, Muli Doshi, erupted in annoyance: &ldquo;Look at these bald Swaminarayan mendicants coming again!&rdquo; She happened to be swabbing the verandah floor with a dirty mop. In a fit of temper, she picked up the filthy, wet mop and hurled it straight at the sadhus! The sadhus swiftly leaned aside, avoiding being hit. Rather than returning anger with abuse, the saintly ascetics collected the discarded rag, carried it back to the riverbank, and said to Muktanand Swami: &ldquo;Swami, today we received no grain in alms, but we received this mop!&rdquo;
Sadguru Muktanand Swami was the very pinnacle of saintliness and forgiving forbearance. Smiling calmly, he advised the ascetics: &ldquo;Wash this rag thoroughly in clean water and unravel its cotton threads into wicks. When evening comes, ignite those wicks to perform the divine arti of Thakorji. Shreeji Maharaj will surely ignite the holy flame of devotion in that woman&rsquo;s heart!&rdquo;
The saints prayed deeply while offering the arti. Touched by the subtle divine vibrations, Muli Doshi experienced an overnight transformation of heart. Overcome with remorse and repentance for her insolence, she hurried to the sadhus early the next morning, sought their pardon, and brought fresh flour and provisions. Being a noble seeker from previous births, her latent spiritual inclinations blossomed swiftly, turning her into a staunch, devoted follower of Satsang. She began gathering village women, passionately extolling the divine glories of Shreeji Maharaj.
Often she would tell her companions with unwavering faith: &ldquo;I may be old and frail, but before my soul departs this mortal frame, my beloved Lord will surely grace my home with His personal darshan!&rdquo;
Some time later, a jubilant, festive marriage procession entered the village of Ghandla. The jingling bells around the bullocks&rsquo; necks echoed melodiously through the lanes. Ascetics adorned in saffron robes sang devotional wedding verses, while driving the ceremonial bullock cart of the bridegroom was the Supreme Lord Shreehari Himself! Hearing the commotion, Muli Doshi joined the village women by the roadside, clutching grains of rice to welcome the procession.
Suddenly, Bhagwan Swaminarayan halted His cart and informed His companions: &ldquo;A beloved devotee in this village yearns for Us; We shall return in a moment.&rdquo; Walking directly towards the women, Shreehari appeared before Muli Doshi. Her heart leaped with boundless joy! Showering Him with consecrated rice, she prostrated in full devotion and prayed tearfully: &ldquo;O Protector of the humble! You have shown unbounded mercy. Pray enter my humble abode!&rdquo;
She escorted Maharaj to her home, prepared a comfortable cot with clean mattresses and bolsters on the verandah, and had her entire family perform His worship. Pleased with her untainted devotion, Shreeji Maharaj declared: &ldquo;Muli Doshi, today We are exceedingly pleased with you; ask for any boon you desire!&rdquo;
With folded hands, she humbly requested: &ldquo;O Maharaj! If You are truly pleased with me, grant that Your holy sadhus may forever reside in this house!&rdquo;
Overhearing this, her worldly husband grumbled from the corner: &ldquo;Senseless woman! You do not even know how to ask for a worthwhile boon! You could have asked for boundless wealth, yet you invited endless toil and hospitality expenses by having sadhus stay forever!&rdquo;
Knowing his cynical thoughts, Maharaj declared with profound authority: &ldquo;The divine wisdom with which this pious lady has asked for a boon cannot be matched by anyone across all fourteen cosmic realms! By securing the eternal presence of holy saints, she has transformed her home into Akshardham itself!&rdquo;
To this day, a sanctified Swaminarayan temple graces that very blessed spot in the village of Ghandla.
