Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Dinanath Bhatt at Dabhan Yajna and Brahmanand Swami&rsquo;s Divine Humor Bhagwan Swaminarayan organized a grand, historic Vishnuyaga Mahayajna in the town of Dabhan. From the elaborate initial arrangements to the grand concluding oblations, the sacred festival spanned nearly two and a half months. Hundreds of ascetics and devoted householders remained anchored at the site throughout the festival, rendering tireless service. Among them was the learned scholar-devotee Dinanath Bhatt, who had been serving devotedly for the entire duration.
With the successful culmination of the yajna, Dinanath Bhatt felt the practical need to return home. His daughter had reached marriageable age, and he had to finalize her betrothal along with managing pressing household responsibilities. Hesitant to approach the Lord directly, he petitioned Sadguru Muktanand Swami: &ldquo;O Swami, two and a half months have elapsed since I arrived here. I urgently need to visit home to arrange my daughter&rsquo;s wedding and attend to pressing worldly duties. Pray seek Shreeji Maharaj&rsquo;s permission on my behalf so that I may depart.&rdquo;
Early that morning, Shreeji Maharaj was seated regally upon the sanctified sacrificial altar (yajna vedi). Sadguru Muktanand Swami approached, offered humble obeisance, and inquired: &ldquo;O Maharaj! Dinanath Bhatt seeks Your gracious leave to return home in order to finalize his daughter&rsquo;s matrimonial alliance and manage urgent family affairs. May he take his departure?&rdquo;
Hearing this domestic request, Shreeji Maharaj assumed the posture of an ultra-austere, unyielding ascetic, delivering a stern lecture on world-renunciation: &ldquo;This entire mundane world is utterly futile, devoid of substance! We possess neither household nor wife; and had We a wife, We would burn her alive in fire! And if children were born to Us, We would haul them away and drown them into the depths of the ocean!&rdquo;
Just as Maharaj uttered these startling words, Sadguru Brahmanand Swami—Maharaj&rsquo;s closest poet-friend known for his matchless wit and divine banter—happened to stroll past. Overhearing Maharaj&rsquo;s melodramatic renunciation, Brahmanand Swami interjected spontaneously without missing a beat: &ldquo;Maharaj! It is precisely because of these terrifying traits of Yours that no father ever dared give you his daughter&rsquo;s hand in marriage! That is why You remained unmarried! And for someone with such cruel intentions, where on earth could a wife and children possibly come from?!&rdquo;
Hearing Brahmanand Swami&rsquo;s sparkling repartee, Shreeji Maharaj, Muktanand Swami, and all the gathered ascetics burst into uncontrollable laughter. The solemn air instantly dissolved into sheer divine joy. Chuckling with immense amusement, Shreeji Maharaj warmly granted Dinanath Bhatt permission to return home and conduct his daughter&rsquo;s wedding festivities with His divine blessings.
