Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The Firm Vow of Hando Koli of Tavi and Initiation by Shreeji Maharaj As Sadguru Gunatitanand Swami declared in his sacred discourses, the supreme Swaminarayan Mahamantra must resound through every leaf and branch. In that very spirit, the early paramhansas of Bhagwan Swaminarayan traveled barefoot from hamlet to hamlet, enduring severe austerities to anchor the roots of Satsang in rural Gujarat.
During one such missionary journey, a group of ascetics arrived at the village of Tavi in the Lakhtar taluka of Surendranagar district. Setting up camp at the local Ramji Mandir, they addressed the village farmers and laborers in the evening, proclaiming with divine fervor: &ldquo;The Supreme Lord of all cosmic realms has manifest in human form! Seek His divine refuge, observe the five moral vows (panch vartaman), and attain eternal salvation in Akshardham.&rdquo; Stirred by their discourses, numerous villagers renounced their vices and accepted the sacred tulsi neck-beads (kanthi).
In that same village lived a simple-minded farmer named Hando Koli. When his fellow villagers urged him to accept initiation from the touring ascetics, Hando replied with rustic obstinacy: &ldquo;You folks may do whatever you like! If Swaminarayan is truly the manifest Supreme Lord in person, then I will accept the sacred beads only directly from His own hands! These sadhus are wonderful, but if their God is genuine, let Him come in person to our village borders and tie the kanthi around my neck Himself!&rdquo;
The sadhus departed after four or five days, yet Hando remained unwavering, often jesting to the locals: &ldquo;You have become disciples through the sadhus, but this man will only be initiated by Swaminarayan Himself!&rdquo;
A short time later, divine providence unfolded. Shreeji Maharaj, riding His renowned mare Manki, happened to pass along the outskirts of Tavi. Devotees working in the surrounding fields ran forward, bowing in reverence and imploring Him to visit their homes. Maharaj replied gently: &ldquo;We are in great haste today, but We shall surely visit another time.&rdquo;
Spotting this, a farmer dashed to Hando&rsquo;s field shouting: &ldquo;Hando! The very Lord Swaminarayan from whom you stubbornly vowed to receive your kanthi is riding by our village boundary on His mare Manki right now!&rdquo;
Dropping his farming implements, Hando ran at full speed, breathless and barefoot. He lunged directly into the pathway of Manki, stretching his arms wide to block the horse. Puffed and earnest, he blurted: &ldquo;Maharaj! I have been eagerly waiting for You for days! Since You are the manifest Supreme Lord, I refuse to be initiated by anyone else; You must tie the sacred beads around my neck with Your own hands!&rdquo;
Captivated by his raw simplicity, unpretentious sincerity, and unwavering determination to meet God face-to-face, Shreeji Maharaj immediately dismounted Manki. Pouring consecrated water into Hando&rsquo;s palm, Maharaj initiated him into the divine refuge and tied the sacred two-stringed tulsi kanthi around his neck.
Having received the initiation, Hando looked up candidly and asked: &ldquo;O Maharaj! Now that You have initiated me as Your follower, what religious vows and strict disciplines am I supposed to observe?&rdquo;
Looking at the unlettered peasant&rsquo;s utter innocence, the compassionate Lord smiled with divine affection. Instilling a foundational virtue of personal cleanliness and ritual hygiene, Maharaj chuckled: &ldquo;Hando! Henceforth, simply ensure you thoroughly wash and cleanse yourself with fresh water every single day after answering nature&rsquo;s call! Do just that, and your eternal liberation is guaranteed!&rdquo;
The gathered onlookers burst into hearty laughter at Maharaj&rsquo;s playful yet practical decree. Through boundless grace, Shreeji Maharaj honored Hando Koli&rsquo;s stubborn devotion and granted him everlasting salvation.
