Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Vadodara&rsquo;s Laddus Fed to Brahmanand Swami in Gadhada by Shreeji Maharaj In Vadodara, when Sadguru Gopalanand Swami arrived at the residence of the noble devotee Narupant Nana to partake of the afternoon meal offering (thal), a spontaneous and heartfelt desire arose in Nana&rsquo;s mind: &ldquo;Sadguru Brahmanand Swami is not present here today, and I cherish immense devotional affection for him. Where could he be at this moment? Had he been here as well, what an unparalleled blessing it would have been for me to serve both great Sadgurus together!&rdquo;
The omniscient Gopalanand Swami instantly perceived Narupant Nana&rsquo;s innermost prayer. During the feast, the sadhus were lovingly served rich laddus and sheera. Afterwards, three large trays (chowkis) piled high with fresh laddus remained untouched. Swami had those trays set aside safely and proceeded to address the spiritual gathering.
Meanwhile, in Gadhpur at the royal Darbargadh of Dada Khachar, Shreeji Maharaj had dined on sweet dudhpak (rich milk pudding) along with the resident saints and had retired for an afternoon rest. At that very moment, Sadguru Brahmanand Swami arrived at the Darbargadh leading a touring group of sixty sadhus, completely exhausted from traversing rural villages. The moment Shreeji Maharaj saw them, He sprang up, warmly embraced Brahmanand Swami, and inquired with boundless love: &ldquo;Swami, have you dined? If you are hungry, what would you like to eat?&rdquo;
Brahmamuni replied with his characteristic wit: &ldquo;O Maharaj! On the way, we have eaten our fill of swirling road dust and blazing desert winds! Now, if we could get some fragrant laddus glistening with pure ghee, our bellies would find true comfort!&rdquo;
Maharaj smiled joyfully and instructed: &ldquo;Sadhus, sit down in a neat row upon the veranda, close your eyes, and chant the divine Narayan dhun with deep devotion; We shall feed you delicious laddus!&rdquo; Through His divine omnipotent power, Shreeji Maharaj instantly transported two full trays of laddus from Narupant Nana’s kitchen in Vadodara to Gadhada. Maharaj personally walked along the row, serving four large laddus onto each sadhu’s plate. After they relished them, Maharaj walked down the line again, lovingly offering two more laddus to each. Maharaj then turned to Brahmanand Swami: &ldquo;Brahmamuni, do you have any further wish?&rdquo; Swami smiled: &ldquo;Maharaj, these dry laddus are hard to swallow; it would be wonderful if You served some liquid accompaniment!&rdquo; Maharaj consulted Jivuba and brought a large clay vessel filled with fresh milk and goras (sweetened curd and buttermilk). He poured it into everyone&rsquo;s bowl, feeding them to their heart&rsquo;s content. Maharaj then playfully poured the remaining buttermilk right over Brahmanand Swami’s head!
Brahmamuni laughed heartily and said: &ldquo;O Maharaj! By drenching my head in sweet buttermilk, You will have swarms of flies hovering over me! It would be best if You come with us right now to bathe in the cool waters of the Ghela river!&rdquo; As evening approached, Maharaj accompanied all the sadhus to the sacred Ghela River, reveling in divine water-sports and showering His devotees with incomparable affection.
Back in Vadodara, Narupant Nana went to the kitchen and was stunned to discover the change. He hurried to Sadguru Gopalanand Swami, asking: &ldquo;Swami, three full trays of laddus were left this afternoon, but now barely half a tray remains! What divine mystery is this?&rdquo;
Gopalanand Swami smilingly disclosed the secret, narrating how Nana&rsquo;s pious desire to feed Brahmanand Swami had been fulfilled at that very instant in Gadhpur by Shreeji Maharaj Himself. Hearing of this divine miracle, Narupant Nana was overwhelmed with devotional joy and fell in reverent prostration at Gopalanand Swami’s holy feet.
