Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Deliverance of a Lame Cat and a Mouse by Sadguru Gopalanand Swami in Vadodara Once, the illustrious Sadguru Gopalanand Swami was gracing the city of Vadodara with his holy presence. The prominent devotee Narupant Nana had arranged a sumptuous feast offering for all the visiting sadhus. Around midday, as Gopalanand Swami stepped out of the temple quarters on his way to partake of the consecrated meal (thal), he encountered a peculiar sight: a lame cat, holding a live mouse firmly clamped between its jaws, was limping its way into the temple grounds.
The accompanying sadhus observed this and remarked with concern, &ldquo;Swami, encountering a cat with prey is conventionally considered an ill omen, and this predator will mercilessly kill the helpless mouse before our eyes. O compassionate Swami! Please bestow your divine grace and ensure the ultimate spiritual well-being of both these souls!&rdquo;
Overflowing with universal compassion, Gopalanand Swami paused, gazed directly at the predator, and commanded with divine authority: &ldquo;Cat! Release the mouse immediately, and from this day forward, never harm or consume any living creature again! Sustain yourself solely by eating the sanctified leftover prasad from the leaf-plates of our holy saints. When you shed this mortal feline body after two years, you shall take birth as a pious human daughter in the household of our devoted disciple Haribhai Kandoi!&rdquo;
Miraculously, hearing the divine voice of the Sadguru, the cat gently laid the unharmed mouse down upon the ground and walked away in peaceful submission. Swami then turned his merciful glance upon the trembling mouse and blessed it: &ldquo;Seek refuge within the nearby shrine of Lord Ganapati; subsist peacefully on the rice grains and sacred offerings made there. When your lifespan concludes, you shall be reborn as a righteous son in the family of our staunch devotee Purushottam Kadiya, where you will attain spiritual liberation!&rdquo;
In this remarkable display of saintly grace, Sadguru Gopalanand Swami not only eradicated the violent animal instincts of the cat and preserved the life of the mouse, but through the transcendental power of devotional association and holy prasad, elevated both lowly creatures into blessed human births among dedicated Satsangi families.
