Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The Chieftain&rsquo;s Palanquin Service in Vadtal Region and Shreehari&rsquo;s Arrival for a Devoted Mother Near the holy town of Vadtal, the aged mother of a village chieftain (Gamdhani Darbar) harbored a deeply emotional and fervent prayer in her heart: &ldquo;If only the merciful Shreeji Maharaj would out of His boundless grace visit our humble home and bestow His divine darshan upon me, my human life would be eternally fulfilled! But alas, owing to severe old age and physical debility, my body cannot endure the arduous journey to Vadtal or Gadhada to behold Him.&rdquo;
Around that time, Shreeji Maharaj was traveling through the villages in the vicinity of Vadtal. At noon, around the customary time for the midday meal offering (thal), Maharaj&rsquo;s footsteps approached the boundary of that very village. A passerby, noticing the radiant procession of the Lord from a distance, sprinted to the Darbargadh and joyfully announced to the chieftain: &ldquo;Darbar! Rejoice, your venerable mother&rsquo;s beloved Bhagwan is walking straight toward our village!&rdquo;
Overjoyed at the sudden arrival of the Lord, the Darbar immediately mobilized to offer a grand reception. However, because of the short notice, he could find only three men to serve as palanquin-bearers to carry Shreeji Maharaj honorably into the village. Without a moment&rsquo;s hesitation or regard for his aristocratic status as the ruler of the village, the chieftain stepped forward and took up the fourth pole of the palanquin upon his own shoulder!
They reached the outskirts of the village, about two kilometers away, where Shreeji Maharaj was walking. Prostrating reverently at Maharaj&rsquo;s sacred lotus feet, the chieftain offered cool refreshing water and humbly beseeched the Lord to ascend the palanquin.
With the chieftain and three attendants carrying the palanquin upon their shoulders, the joyful party began the journey back to the village. Observing the noble chieftain bearing the heavy weight upon his own shoulder under the afternoon sun, compassionate Shreeji Maharaj leaned out and urged: &ldquo;Darbar! Please step aside and do not carry this load. We will gladly walk on foot alongside you into the village!&rdquo;
Tears of pure devotional love welled in the chieftain&rsquo;s eyes. In an attitude of absolute surrender and humility, he responded: &ldquo;O Maharaj! Throughout countless previous incarnations—wandering through the bodies of camels, bullocks, and beasts of burden—this soul has borne innumerable agonizing worldly loads! Today, by immense fortune, I have received the once-in-a-lifetime opportunity to carry the Supreme Lord of infinite realms, Purushottam Narayan Himself! Does such a divine privilege ever come again and again in every life? Pray do not deprive me of this supreme grace!&rdquo;
Deeply moved by the chieftain&rsquo;s humility, devotion, and profound spiritual wisdom, Shreeji Maharaj smiled radiantly and remarked: &ldquo;Darbar, it is truly the pure, unadulterated love of your revered mother that has drawn Us all the way to your village today!&rdquo;
Upon entering the village, Maharaj graced the home of the chieftain, granted His divine vision to the jubilant elderly mother, fulfilled her lifelong yearning, and sanctified the entire family with His divine blessings.
