Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Ladudoshi&rsquo;s Offering of Wild Greens near Lakshmivadi and Service to Manki in Gadhpur One afternoon in Gadhpur, after enjoying a refreshing holy bath in the sacred waters of the Ghela River near Lakshmivadi, Shreeji Maharaj mounted His celebrated divine mare, Manki, to ride back to the royal Darbargadh. Accompanying Him were the beloved chieftain Sura Khachar (Sura Bapu), Sadguru Brahmanand Swami, and several close attendants.
Near the entrance of Lakshmivadi stood a humble thatched hut where an impoverished, elderly widow named Ladudoshi lived entirely alone. Belonging to the Koli community, she had no relatives or worldly resources to support her fragile old age. As Shreeji Maharaj&rsquo;s royal party rode past, Ladudoshi hurried forward with trembling hands, offering a bundle of freshly gathered wild greens (tandalja bhaji) wrapped inside the folds of her worn sari. With tears streaming down her wrinkled cheeks, she pleaded: &ldquo;O Bhagwan Swaminarayan! Pray accept this humble wild tandalja greens from me, so that this destitute life of mine may attain spiritual fruition!&rdquo;
Beholding her pure, unblemished affection, the compassionate Lord Shreeji Maharaj was deeply touched. Reining in Manki, He leaned forward, accepted the wild greens with His own holy hands, and affectionately encouraged her: &ldquo;Mother! You have lovingly fed Us greens; ask of Us whatever boon your heart desires!&rdquo;
Without a second thought, the pious woman folded her hands in utter surrender and prayed: &ldquo;O Almighty Lord! Wandering endlessly through the terrifying wilderness of worldly transmigration (bhavatavi), I have become thoroughly exhausted! I seek no ephemeral comforts; please, this time, grant me eternal liberation and take me into Your supreme abode!&rdquo;
Hearing this loftiest of prayers from such a destitute woman, Sura Bapu chuckled softly. Brahmanand Swami noticed and inquired, &ldquo;Bapu, why did you laugh?&rdquo;
Sura Bapu whispered amusingly, &ldquo;Swami! This poor old woman has not a morsel of grain in her house, nor anyone to nurse her failing health. Before asking for the ultimate liberation, she ought to have first secured her daily bread for this earthly life!&rdquo;
Overhearing their exchange, omniscient Shreeji Maharaj turned to Sura Bapu and remarked with profound wisdom: &ldquo;Sura Bapu, you fail to grasp the supreme wisdom of this old mother! In a single stroke, she has obtained everything imaginable from Us today!&rdquo;
Maharaj then turned to Ladudoshi and pronounced His divine ordinance: &ldquo;Mother, starting tomorrow morning, come daily to the Darbargadh and perform the sacred service of sweeping and cleaning the stable of our divine mare, Manki. As long as you dwell upon this earth, Laduba and Jivuba will lovingly serve you warm, sanctified rotlas for both your meals; and when your lifespan is finished, We personally will come to escort you to Our eternal abode of Akshardham!&rdquo;
Overwhelmed with awe and veneration, Brahmanand Swami and Sura Bapu marveled aloud: &ldquo;O Lord! Truly, this blessed woman has secured the triple crown of spiritual fortune in an instant—the sacred physical seva of Muktaraj Manki, daily consecrated meals directly from the holy hands of Laduba and Jivuba, and eternal liberation in Akshardham!&rdquo;
